  "id": "Compound::DB00936 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Salicylic Acid is implicated in the regulation of Slc22a11 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the sodium-independent organic anion transporter activity. The evidence suggests that Salicylic Acid binds to Slco2b1 and Slc22a7, both of which are involved in the transport of organic anions across cellular membranes. This binding likely modulates the activity of these transporters, which in turn influence the expression or function of Slc22a11. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, with varying levels of confidence in the mechanistic link. The shared involvement of Slc22a7 in the transport process across different paths strengthens the hypothesis that Salicylic Acid exerts its effect through a common pathway involving the sodium-independent organic anion transporter. The integration of these findings supports the idea that Salicylic Acid may regulate Slc22a11 by modulating the activity of the sodium-independent organic anion transporter, potentially through a mechanism that involves the transport of organic anions and their impact on cellular homeostasis.",
